{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}About — StreamList{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="ab-page">
    <section class="ab-card">
        <h2>What it does</h2>
        <p>
            StreamList is a watchlist-first movie app. Browse a catalog seeded from
            TMDB, filter by genre, and queue what you want to see. Free accounts hold
            20 titles; premium lifts the cap. When you're ready for more, send an
            upgrade request and an admin reviews it — no self-serve payment, just
            a human in the loop.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ab-card">
        <h2>How it's built</h2>
        <p>
            The application runs on Symfony with Doctrine talking to MySQL.
            Pages are rendered server-side with Twig; authentication uses
            Symfony's security layer with CSRF-protected forms throughout.
            Movie data, posters, and trailers come from TMDB; cast and crew
            are stored locally so detail pages stay fast.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ab-card">
        <h2>Found a problem?</h2>
        <p>
            Bugs and movie suggestions are welcome through the contact page —
            messages land straight in the admin inbox. (That page is coming
            back to this app soon.)
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
{% endblock %}